{
  "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two large, vibrant red bell pepper halves positioned side-by-side on two separate matte ceramic plates. The pepper halves are centered in the frame, angled at a 3/4 overhead perspective to reveal the generous mound of filling inside. Each pepper is overflowing with a colorful mix of shredded rotisserie chicken, fluffy quinoa, and bright, quartered cherry tomatoes. The roughly chopped baby spinach is wilted and integrated throughout the quinoa, adding deep green tones, while pieces of chopped dark Kalamata olives are tucked into the mixture. The surface of each pepper is crowned with rustic, uneven crumbles of white feta cheese. The lighting is soft and natural, coming from a window to the left, highlighting the succulent texture of the chicken and the slight sheen of olive oil and lemon juice on the filling. The background is a warm, aged oak kitchen table with a soft bokeh. Props include a single wooden fork resting casually next to one plate and a small, slightly messy pile of quinoa grains and a lone Kalamata olive piece scattered on the wooden surface. The second plate is softly blurred in the background, showing the complete serving for two. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene reflects a home-cooked meal, warm and authentic, not a studio setup. Slight natural imperfections: a small sauce drip on one plate rim, unevenly placed feta crumbles, and a natural, lived-in feel. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces. No text, no watermark, no hands, no faces."
}
